Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: web888-ng-hw
Source: https://github.com/jeskko/web888-ng-hw
Comment:
 Pinned to tag v0.3.0 (annotated tag 8b7ab5061ad6be5cd24322dd8912b6551e25350a,
 commit 767030740a2fdecfebdd383efd23330e6455ff1b). The shipped .bit files are
 the upstream v0.3.0 release assets (CI-built with Vivado 2026.1 from that
 tag; asset hashes pinned in config/web888-ng/pins.env and re-verified
 against the upstream SHA256SUMS asset at build time). Building Vivado from
 source is not possible on this infrastructure; the upstream CI artifacts
 are used as-is with their published digests.
 .
 The channelizer bitstream (websdr_pfb.bit) is deliberately NOT shipped: it
 needs the open driver, while these two target the stock-compatible
 register map served by the web888-redpitaya kernel driver.

